From df2261597ccc577abbf2b96c8682b5bb7b2f3c72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FVOCI <150913557+fvoci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:18:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(events): Escape cancels the clash prompt and save-mine
 merges onto the newest version (D-94 review)

Escape on the "overwrite?" prompt reached the dialog and closed it, so
the unsaved input was lost. While the prompt is shown Escape now only
withdraws it, like Cancel: nothing is sent, the input stays and focus
returns to "Save mine again".

When overwrite got another 409 or the save went through, the pressed
button disappeared and focus fell to the dialog. It now moves, a frame
later as in TaskDetail, to "Save mine again" of the refreshed notice or
to the dialog heading (the saved title).

Saving a recurrence rule while the notice is shown returns a newer
version than the notice held, and save-mine merged onto the older one,
which the server always refused. The notice, the merge and "Load their
version" now use whichever of the two is newer. Overwrite goes ahead
when the asked units and both shown values are unchanged, so a rule
save in between does not ask again.

Titles and descriptions are compared trimmed, as the server stores
them, so adding spaces is not an edit that reverts or clashes with
someone else's change. The clash label names the whole unit including
all-day. EventForm only gains a comment that onsubmit must run before
its first await (EventDialog tells a save-mine submit by a flag held
during requestSubmit()).

Test: event-save-mine (Escape, focus after 409 and save, rule save
during the notice, validation-blocked save-mine leaves the next save
plain) and event-conflict-merge (trimmed comparison).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
